      "source_skill_name": "dev-execution",
      "task_class": "implementation",
      "roles": {
        "orchestrator": "orchestration",
        "implementer": "implementation"
      },
      "rationale": "DUAL-ROLE. The orchestrator loads dev-execution (/dev:execute-phase, /dev:execute-plan) and so do the implementer legs it dispatches, so a skill-only key folds MUST-stay orchestration spend into a demotable class. Measured 2026-08-11: 164 orchestrator-role Opus sessions (8.4% of them) carried 62.4% of all Opus dev-execution cost, avg $178/session against $9-13 for the other roles. Orchestrator-role rows now resolve to `orchestration`, which is protected and therefore dropped from the rollup; only implementer-role rows feed `implementation`. `task_class` remains the role-blind fallback and the only class this rule can emit into feedback."
    },
